description:
Implement `useCanvas` — a hook that attaches to a `<canvas>` element and provides the 2D rendering context along with utility functions.

- `ref` — attach to a `<canvas>` element
- `ctx` — the `CanvasRenderingContext2D` (null before mount)
- `clear()` — fills the canvas with white
- `getImageData()` — returns the full canvas ImageData

**Example:**
```tsx
function DrawingBoard() {
  const { ref, ctx, clear } = useCanvas();

  const draw = () => {
    if (!ctx) return;
    ctx.fillStyle = 'red';
    ctx.fillRect(10, 10, 50, 50);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <canvas ref={ref} width={300} height={200} />
      <button onClick={draw}>Draw</button>
      <button onClick={clear}>Clear</button>
    </>
  );
}
```

